<h1>Typography</h1>

<p class="l-ui-utility--mt-md">layered-ui-rails applies base typography styles to standard HTML elements via <code>@layer base</code>, so they can be overridden by the host application. Headings use the Manrope font and body text uses Inter.</p>

<h2 class="l-ui-utility--mt-2xl">Headings</h2>

<div class="l-ui-surface l-ui-utility--mt-lg">
  <h1>Heading 1</h1>
  <h2 class="l-ui-utility--mt-lg">Heading 2</h2>
  <h3 class="l-ui-utility--mt-lg">Heading 3</h3>
</div>

<div class="l-ui-utility--mt-xl" data-controller="l-ui--modal">
  <button class="l-ui-button--outline" data-action="l-ui--modal#open">View code</button>
  <dialog class="l-ui-modal" data-l-ui--modal-target="dialog" data-action="click->l-ui--modal#closeOnBackdrop" aria-labelledby="modal-typography-headings-heading">
    <div class="l-ui-modal__header">
      <h3 id="modal-typography-headings-heading">Headings</h3>
      <button class="l-ui-button--icon" data-action="l-ui--modal#close" aria-label="Close">
        <svg class="l-ui-icon--sm" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M6 18L18 6M6 6l12 12"></path>
        </svg>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class="l-ui-modal__body">
      <code class="l-ui-surface">&lt;h1&gt;Heading 1&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Heading 2&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Heading 3&lt;/h3&gt;</code>
    </div>
  </dialog>
</div>

<h2 class="l-ui-utility--mt-2xl">Paragraphs</h2>

<div class="l-ui-surface l-ui-utility--mt-lg">
  <p>This is a standard paragraph. Body text uses the Inter font at a small size with relaxed line height and muted foreground color.</p>
  <p class="l-ui-utility--mt-md">Paragraphs can contain <a href="#">inline links</a> which are styled with an underline and use the foreground color.</p>
</div>

